[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/comments/4120673393","html_url":"https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/issues/21592#issuecomment-4120673393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/21592","id":4120673393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCEU65s71nHxx","user":{"login":"hawkfish","id":13156216,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTU2MjE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13156216?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish","html_url":"https://github.com/hawkfish","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-24T19:00:03Z","updated_at":"2026-03-24T19:00:03Z","body":"Hi @Flamefork  - Thanks for the report. Should be a simple fix, but for now you can disable the optimisation with:\n\n```sql\nSET disabled_optimizers = 'window_self_join';\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/comments/4120673393/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/comments/4130136929","html_url":"https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/issues/21592#issuecomment-4130136929","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/21592","id":4130136929,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCEU65s72LONh","user":{"login":"hawkfish","id":13156216,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTU2MjE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13156216?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish","html_url":"https://github.com/hawkfish","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-25T22:05:22Z","updated_at":"2026-03-25T22:05:22Z","body":"Note that the result here is not well defined (you are asking for a running sum over an unsorted partition.)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/comments/4130136929/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/comments/4182367549","html_url":"https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/issues/21592#issuecomment-4182367549","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/21592","id":4182367549,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCEU65s75Sd09","user":{"login":"Whatsonyourmind","id":248369826,"node_id":"U_kgDODs3Sog","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/248369826?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind","html_url":"https://github.com/Whatsonyourmind","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-03T07:45:48Z","updated_at":"2026-04-09T13:31:23Z","body":"Good root cause analysis. To clarify the semantics for anyone else reading:\n\nThe SQL standard defines two frame types with different \\\"peer\\\" semantics:\n\n- **RANGE frame**: rows with equal ORDER BY values are \\\"peers\\\" and treated as a group. Without ORDER BY, all partition rows are peers, so UNBOUNDED PRECEDING to CURRENT ROW covers the entire partition.\n- **ROWS frame**: every row is distinct regardless of ORDER BY values. CURRENT ROW means literally that single row.\n\nSo `ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW` *without* ORDER BY should still produce cumulative results (each row gets a running sum up to its physical position), just in nondeterministic order since the row ordering within the partition is unspecified.\n\nThe \\`CanOptimize\\` check in \\`window_self_join.cpp\\` should additionally verify that the frame endpoints are truly whole-partition:\n\n```cpp\nbool is_full_partition = \n    w_expr.start == WindowBoundary::UNBOUNDED_PRECEDING &&\n    (w_expr.end == WindowBoundary::UNBOUNDED_FOLLOWING ||\n     (w_expr.end == WindowBoundary::CURRENT_ROW_RANGE && w_expr.orders.empty()));\n```\n\nThis mirrors the more conservative check already in \\`WindowConstantAggregator::CanAggregate\\`.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/comments/4182367549/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/comments/4184038012","html_url":"https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/issues/21592#issuecomment-4184038012","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/21592","id":4184038012,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCEU65s75Y1p8","user":{"login":"hawkfish","id":13156216,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTU2MjE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13156216?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish","html_url":"https://github.com/hawkfish","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkfish/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-03T15:54:42Z","updated_at":"2026-04-03T15:54:42Z","body":"The standard also defines `GROUPS` framing, which has similar peer semantics to `RANGE`, except that instead of choosing peers based on a distance metric, it chooses them by a simple count of the peers. Accepting `GROUPS` in this context is an extension to the standard, and it has the same \"constant\" semantics as `RANGE`.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/comments/4184038012/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/comments/4199270107","html_url":"https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/issues/21592#issuecomment-4199270107","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/21592","id":4199270107,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCEU65s76S8bb","user":{"login":"Whatsonyourmind","id":248369826,"node_id":"U_kgDODs3Sog","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/248369826?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind","html_url":"https://github.com/Whatsonyourmind","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Whatsonyourmind/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-07T13:22:38Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T13:22:38Z","body":"@hawkfish Good addition on GROUPS framing — I had not included it in the original comment and it is worth the documentation thread. The peer-counting semantics of GROUPS is the cleanest way to explain why `GROUPS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW` produces a constant across peer groups (exactly the same constancy property as RANGE, just measured in peer-group counts rather than value distances). The only place GROUPS and RANGE diverge in practice is when the ORDER BY is over a non-numeric type where \"distance\" is not well-defined — GROUPS handles strings and enums gracefully while RANGE requires a numeric or date/time expression.\n\nThe fact that DuckDB accepts GROUPS at all is an extension to SQL:2003 that most engines still do not support — PostgreSQL added it in v11, but Spark, Snowflake, and ClickHouse still do not. Worth flagging in the docs that GROUPS is DuckDB-specific in the window frame grammar, because users migrating from other engines will not realize it is available.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/comments/4199270107/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]